      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "e3bsacl8",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Midjourney Character Reference vs. Lovart Nano Banana: Consistency Test"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "img-aeb7ee52",
      "_type": "imageSource",
      "alt": "Lovart selecting ai models feature screenshot",
      "sourceType": "external",
      "url": "https://cdn.sanity.io/images/o11tm2qe/production/831a2192ac4eb19dacf6f6a50017b6c8fb60e05b-2160x1350.jpg"
    },
    {
      "_key": "f6hfp2bl",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "k50z3cu0",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "For artists, storytellers, and brand builders, the holy grail of AI image generation is "
        },
        {
          "_key": "7ucq19tk",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "character consistency"
        },
        {
          "_key": "jrbxsao7",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". The ability to render the same fictional person—with the same face, hairstyle, clothing style, and physical proportions—across multiple scenes, angles, and lighting conditions is what transforms a collection of pretty pictures into a coherent visual narrative or a recognizable brand asset. Two of the most advanced approaches to this challenge are embodied by different tools: Midjourney’s "
        },
        {
          "_key": "dc5exslu",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Character Reference"
        },
        {
          "_key": "5i81a2yo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " feature and the generative capabilities powered by models like "
        },
        {
          "_key": "mlbnu5mo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Nano Banana"
        },
        {
          "_key": "q1k7wyp5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " within "
        },
        {
          "_key": "rjirkp16",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "link1"
          ],
          "text": "Lovart’s ChatCanvas"
        },
        {
          "_key": "7e7zg9r5",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ". Both aim to solve the same core problem, but they do so through fundamentally different technological and philosophical pathways. Midjourney’s method is one of "
        },
        {
          "_key": "7bwow97s",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "visual anchoring"
        },
        {
          "_key": "aa2del31",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "—using an uploaded image as a rigid guide. Lovart’s approach, particularly when leveraging the nuanced understanding of a model like Nano Banana within its "
        },
        {
          "_key": "nfyim0ro",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Design Agent"
        },
        {
          "_key": "pb6xdo8o",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " framework, is one of "
        },
        {
          "_key": "saoxbbtx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "semantic and stylistic governance"
        },
        {
          "_key": "fsqaoamo",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "—defining a character through a system of descriptive and relational rules. This comparative analysis puts these two methods to the test, examining not just which can produce a similar face twice, but which can maintain the integrity of a character as a believable entity across a dynamic, narrative-driven series of images ."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [
