    {
      "_key": "ncfxhvif",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "ktmu8ehd",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The quest for character consistency reveals a deeper divide in AI design philosophy. Midjourney seeks to replicate a specific visual arrangement. "
        },
        {
          "_key": "vjoo4ijx",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "link2"
          ],
          "text": "Lovart"
        },
        {
          "_key": "lp1l5wks",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", through the conversational and structural framework of the "
        },
        {
          "_key": "1qvd3g1e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "ChatCanvas"
        },
        {
          "_key": "kub47183",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": " and tools like "
        },
        {
          "_key": "guais4uh",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ],
          "text": "Edit Elements"
        },
        {
          "_key": "wthge52b",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": ", seeks to establish and maintain a coherent entity within a governed visual system.\nFor creating a series of profile pictures or static variations, the anchor method is sufficient. For building a storyboard, a comic, a game asset pipeline, or a brand campaign where a character must live, breathe, and adapt across a narrative arc, the systemic governance of Lovart—where consistency is managed through semantic definition, style rules, and intelligent asset reuse—provides a fundamentally more robust and flexible solution. It tests not the AI’s ability to copy a face, but its capacity to understand and preserve a role."
        }
      ],
